    <div
      class="MuiPaper-root MuiPaper-page MuiPaper-rounded css-i0wy4-MuiPaper-root"
    >
      <h1
        class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
      >
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <div
        class="MuiBox-root css-av31co"
      >
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Effective Date:
          </strong>
           January 1, 2022
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Last Updated:
          </strong>
           November 25, 2026
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          Bldrs Share (“we,” “us,” “our”) provides open-source, browser-first tools for viewing and collaborating on 3D model files (e.g., IFC, STEP) using our Conway Engine. We design our software to minimize data collection and maximize user control.
        </p>
        <h1
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          1. Information We Collect
        </h1>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          Bldrs Share operates 
          <strong>
            without centralized model data storage
          </strong>
          . We do not upload or host user model data by default. What we do receive:
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Authentication data.
          </strong>
           When you sign in via Auth0/Google or another provider, we receive basic profile information (name, email, avatar) to create or identify your account.
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Model data.
          </strong>
           Models you open are processed locally in your browser using WebAssembly. If you connect third-party storage (e.g., Google Drive), we only request access to the specific files you select. We do not scan or store other files from your account.
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Error and reliability reports.
          </strong>
           When something fails, the app reports what failed, the app and browser versions and the address of the page you were on to our error-monitoring service (Sentry). For a model opened from GitHub, Google Drive or a web address, that page address includes where the model is. Reports from our servers also carry your account ID when you’re signed in. Separately, the app counts browsers that can’t run part of it (for example, with no WebGL) by browser family and device type only, sent to Google Analytics from our server under one shared ID rather than yours. None of these reports set cookies, carry an identifier that follows your browser between visits, or include your models’ contents. Sentry keeps them for at most 90 days. They are part of operating the service and are always on, on the basis of our legitimate interest in keeping Bldrs Share secure and working.
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            How models load.
          </strong>
           There is no Google Analytics or other tracking code in the app: no analytics cookies, and no identifier that follows your browser between visits. To learn how Bldrs Share is used and how it performs, the app reports each model you open to our server: the kind of file, its size range, where it came from (your computer, GitHub, Google Drive or a web address), whether it was the first model on the page, how long it took to load, how complex it was, roughly how many errors and warnings it raised, whether it loaded or failed and at what stage, and whether you’re on a phone or a computer. A report never includes a model’s name, path, web address or contents; the only model it names is one of our own sample models, if that’s what you opened. It carries one random ID that lives only while the page is open, so the models opened in one visit can be counted together; it is never stored, and a reload starts a new one. The app also reports each time you open a page: what kind of page it was (the home page, or the viewer and where its model comes from), what kind of site you came from (a search engine, a social network, our own site, another site, or none), a campaign name only if it is one we know, and whether you’re on a phone or a computer. It never includes the page’s address or the site you came from, and it carries the same random ID, so a visit can be counted with the models opened in it. Our server adds your country, as its hosting provider locates the request, and keeps it nowhere. Our server passes these reports on to Google Analytics under one shared ID, so Google never sees your browser or network address. They are always on, on the basis of our legitimate interest in running and improving the service.
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Your account’s usage.
          </strong>
           If you’re signed in, the report of each model you open is also kept with your account, so we can see how much each account uses Bldrs Share and how it performs for them: the same kind of file, size range, where it came from, whether it loaded and how long it took, with how complex it was rounded and your plan. Like every report, it never includes a model’s name, path, web address or contents. We use it to run and improve the service, on the basis of our legitimate interest in doing so. Your account’s records are kept for 13 months, then reduced to totals that name no account. To turn this off, use “Use my usage to improve Bldrs” in the Profile menu; turning it off also deletes the records already kept. Records of when your account reaches a free-use limit are kept either way, for the same 13 months, because they are part of applying the limits. Sign-ins and upgrade clicks are counted in Google Analytics from our server under one shared ID, never yours.
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Free-use limits.
          </strong>
           Some features have a free allowance. If you’re signed in, your account keeps a record of the private models you’ve opened (which model, and when) for as long as the current limit window needs it, to apply your plan’s limits; if you subscribe, it also lists the models you’ve exported so you can find them again. If you use the AI assistant without signing in, your browser keeps a random ID our server issued, which expires after 24 hours, and our server keeps a keyed hash of your network address for the day, never the address itself. Both are used only to apply the free allowance and to stop abuse.
        </p>
        <h1
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          2. Open-Source and Self-Hosted Use
        </h1>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          Most of our codebase (including Bldrs Share and Conway) is available under the
          <strong>
             GNU Affero General Public License (AGPL)
          </strong>
           on GitHub. If you deploy or modify our software, you are responsible for complying with applicable privacy laws and for communicating your own deployment’s data-handling practices to your users.
        </p>
        <h1
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          3. How We Use Information
        </h1>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          We use limited account and usage data to authenticate users; enable integrations (e.g., importing from Google Drive); improve performance, security, and usability; and communicate important service updates.
        </p>
        <h1
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          4. Data Storage and Security
        </h1>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            No persistent model storage by default.
          </strong>
           Model data is processed client-side and is not uploaded to our servers. Communication between your browser and our services uses HTTPS. Future, optional hosted collaboration features (e.g., Firestore for comments/sharing) may store limited user-generated data; if launched, this policy will be updated accordingly.
        </p>
        <h1
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          5. Google User Data
        </h1>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          Our use of Google user data complies with the
           
          <a
            class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-inherit MuiLink-root MuiLink-underlineAlways css-1onfuse-MuiTypography-root-MuiLink-root"
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            rel="noopener"
            target="_blank"
          >
            Google API Services User Data Policy
          </a>
          , including Limited Use requirements. Access to Google Drive is used solely to open or save the files that you explicitly select.
        </p>
        <h1
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          6. Your Choices
        </h1>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          You can disconnect Google access in your Google Account settings. You may request deletion of any stored account metadata (if applicable) by emailing 
          <a
            class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-inherit MuiLink-root MuiLink-underlineAlways css-1onfuse-MuiTypography-root-MuiLink-root"
            href="mailto:support@bldrs.ai"
          >
            support@bldrs.ai
          </a>
          . You can also use open-source/self-hosted deployments without accounts, subject to your configuration.
        </p>
        <h1
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          7. Children’s Privacy
        </h1>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          Our services are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.
        </p>
        <h1
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
